Proposed verification criteria:
1. When the website is accessed with a preview/draft content indication, the page renders content from the draft version of the entry rather than the published version.
2. When the website is accessed without any preview/draft indication, all content renders from published entries — behavior is identical to current production behavior with no visual or functional regression.
3. Given the Contentstack API is mocked to return draft content for a page entry containing rich text, images, and component blocks, the website renders those elements using the draft data, displaying the same layout and component structure used for published content.
